{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And the men came upon the women\"</b> is that the freewill offering of ornaments is more common among women, and they all had them, and they removed their nose-rings and their rings from their hands at once, and they came first, and the men who had them brought them along, for the meaning of \"upon the women\" is that they were there first and the men were secondary to them. And similarly, \"Aram is set upon Ephraim\" (Isaiah 7:2), for that war was directed against Ephraim; \"and he did not set them upon Laban's flock\" (Genesis 30:40); \"and upon him the tribe of Manasseh\" (Numbers 2:20), and similar verses. And he said that all of them came, men and women, with חַח and nose-ring and ring and כּוּמָז, and with every article of gold such as bracelets and earrings, for all of them possessed ornamental articles. And he said that among them were some who waved the wave-offering of broken gold or in coin." "And he said, <b>\"And every man with whom was found תְּכֵלֶת and אַרְגָּמָן\"</b> — for these were found only among some of them. And he went back and said, <b>\"with whom was found wood of שִׁטִּים\"</b> — for those who had wood of שִׁטִּים in their possession were even fewer. And he said, <b>\"all who raised the offering of silver and bronze\"</b> — for most people had silver and bronze in coins and vessels, but he did not mention these above (Exodus 35:22) together with the gold articles, because there he mentioned the women, and they do not have silver and bronze but only gold in ornaments, as he said (Exodus 32:2), \"the gold rings which are in your wives' ears.\"" "<b>\"And every man who waved a wave-offering of gold\"</b> — they were not as numerous as those who raised silver and bronze, and the bringing of gold was not as plentiful as silver and bronze; therefore this is called תְּנוּפָה (wave-offering) and that is called תְּרוּמָה (raising/offering), for the one who brings gold waves his hand for the importance of the gift, or those who receive it wave the gold to display it, to praise the one who brings it for his freewill offering. And in the portion אֵלֶּה פְקוּדֵי (further below, 38:24, 29) the gold and also the bronze will be called תְּנוּפָה, because there he did not mention תְּרוּמָה at all (Exodus 35:25–28), only \"the silver of those numbered of the congregation.\" And it is possible that the bronze too will be called תְּנוּפָה because it was more valuable to them than silver, since it was not readily available in their possession. Or because it was very highly valued, as in the matter stated (Ezra 8:27), \"and vessels of bronze, fine burnished, two, precious as gold.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:50.106139888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}